# A known bug of pulsar-client-go v0.21.0 (RESULTS.md, finding 1; pulsar-client-go#1498, with the
# open pull request 1499). The image of hydo.yaml has the client with pull request 1499 (the
# build parameter client=fix), and this run without faults passes: no aborted transaction's
# message is delivered. Built with --set client=release (pulsar-client-go v0.21.0) the same run
# fails on every run: the client writes the transaction's id into the send command only, not
# into the message's metadata, and the broker's dispatcher filters aborted messages by the
# metadata (AbstractBaseDispatcher), so every message of an aborted transaction is delivered:
#   VIOLATION [txn] 3 of 16 transactions not all or nothing: 0 committed, 3 aborted, 0 unknown
# (fp=8cf005d04d8a1961 on the image built with --set client=release --out .hydo-release)
# expect: ok      (with --set client=release: violation)
disk=none | run
